# Who reviews the documentation.
#
# GitHub auto-requests a review from these owners on any pull request touching a matching
# path. It is advisory: it blocks nothing unless "Require review from Code Owners" is
# switched on in branch protection, which it is not. The point is that a second person sees
# a change to the pages other repos — and other agents — rely on.
#
# Which docs cover which code is a separate question, answered by .docs-map.yml. This file
# only says who looks at the docs themselves.
#
# Spec: https://tech.helloally.ai/#/wiki/contributing/docs-system.md

/*.md                        @HelloAllyTech/helloallydevs
/.docs-map.yml               @HelloAllyTech/helloallydevs
/.github/pull_request_template.md  @HelloAllyTech/helloallydevs
/docs/                       @HelloAllyTech/helloallydevs
